  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.9.8 — MCP support, agentic robustness, and live shell streaming\n\nAdded:\n- MCP (Model Context Protocol) support — connect to any MCP server (stdio or remote HTTP/SSE), tools auto-registered alongside built-in plugins. Interactive `/mcp add` wizard, per-tool first-use approval, `/mcp`, `/mcp tools`, `/mcp remove`, `/mcp-reload`.\n- Skills — user-defined skill packs (a folder containing a SKILL.md file) that the model can auto-invoke based on name/description via the new `load_skill(name)` function. Loaded from `~/.mandocode/skills/` and project-local `./.mandocode/skills/`. New `/skills` slash command lists installed skills.\n- propose_plan tool — models self-classify multi-step requests via a Semantic Kernel function instead of a separate planning round-trip; ~300 lines of fragile text-parsing removed.\n- Per-turn circuit breakers, auto-continuation, and synthetic-summary recovery on context-window overflow — long agentic loops no longer silently hang or crash.\n- Streaming execute_command — shell tool now streams stdout/stderr line-by-line; the spinner shows live `$ <cmd> → <latest line>` activity.\n- Idle-based shell timeout — replaces the old 30s wall-clock kill with a 30s idle timeout (kills only after 30s of no output) plus a 10-minute hard ceiling. Long legitimate builds now run to completion as long as they're emitting output.\n- Configurable per-request timeout (`requestTimeoutMinutes`, default 15), tool-result char budget (`toolResultCharBudget`, default 100k), and markdown render timeout (`markdownRenderTimeoutSeconds`, default 60).\n- Shell-aware system prompt — detects cmd.exe vs bash and stops the model from emitting `head`/`grep`/`cat` on Windows.\n\nUI:\n- Spinner shows elapsed time and rotates its random message every 15s during long waits.\n- Live activity row above the spinner (used by streamed shell output, plan steps, MCP tools); persists in scrollback after the spinner stops if it was ever updated.\n- Inline auto-continuation and overflow-recovery markers so automatic restarts are visible instead of silent.\n- New plan approval UI (Execute / Reject / Cancel) replaces the old \"Analyzing...\" spinner phase.\n- Tighter markdown / HTML rendering — reworked renderer produces noticeably more compact output for headings, bullets, and tables, plus a refreshed color palette.\n\nChanged:\n- Default per-request timeout raised from 5 min to 15 min.\n- AIService constructor signature gained PlanHandoff and SpinnerService; FileSystemPlugin constructor gained an optional SpinnerService.\n\nFixed:\n- Paste with newlines no longer auto-submits the prompt before the user finishes editing.\n- Keystrokes typed during diff-approval \"additional instructions\" prompts are no longer dropped by the parent input loop.",
